    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full `./mvnw test` run is green (2/2 passing, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe locality derivation now prefers the postcode, falling back to the city table.\n\n**Changes (2 files):**\n\n1. **New `Locality.java`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 a small helper with one public `locality(Owner)` method plus a private `byPostcode` helper. It looks up the region by postcode range first (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099), and only falls back to the `CITY_REGION` table (\u2192 `UNKNOWN` if absent) when the postcode is null, not four digits, or in no known range.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java:25`** \u2014 replaced the inline city-only ternary chain with a single delegating call `Locality.locality(owner)`, mirroring the existing pattern on line 27 (`CheckUniqueIdentity.identityKey(owner)`).\n\n**Why this keeps structural impact low:** the mapper edit is a single line, and its complexity *dropped* (a nested ternary became one call), so the costly `toOwnerDto` change stays minimal. All the new branching lives in a fresh, cohesive class with `WMC_other = 0`, rather than growing the already-large mapper method.\n\nKnown cities still resolve to the same region (Sydney/2000 \u2192 NSW), while cities that share a name are now disambiguated by postcode \u2014 verified by `functionalityPostcodePreferredOverCity` (unknown city + postcode 3000 \u2192 VIC).",
