    "probe_text": "Here's the complete ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners`. Every step runs under a single write transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]` on all steps), so the whole thing commits once at the end. Marked **[V]** for validations (can reject the request) and **[S]** for side-effects (mutations/persistence/output).\n\n## Guard (before any step)\n- **[V] Authorization** \u2014 the endpoint file requires `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`; without it the request is denied (`AuthorizationDeniedException`).\n\n## 1. `BuildOwner` (reads the `@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` \u2014 the only body-binding step)\n- **[S]** Publishes a `sharesHousehold` boolean (from `request.getSharesHousehold()`) for later steps.\n- **[S]** Normalizes the address via `AddressNormalizer`: trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand abbreviations (`ST`\u2192`STREET`, `RD`\u2192`ROAD`, `AVE`\u2192`AVENUE`); null/blank \u2192 `\"\"`.\n- **[V]** Requires `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (post-normalization), `city`, `telephone` all non-null and non-blank \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException(missing fields)`.\n- **[S]** Maps DTO \u2192 `Owner`. During mapping, `registrationDate` **defaults to today** if not supplied (`OwnerMapper.toOwner`).\n- **[S/V]** Normalizes telephone to E.164 (`+` keeps country code; otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0`; strips spaces/dashes/brackets). If the national-number length is invalid \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException(\"telephone\")`; otherwise sets the normalized value.\n- **[S]** Sets the normalized address on the owner.\n- **[V]** If `email` is present, it must match the email regex \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException(\"email\")`.\n- **[S]** Publishes the built `Owner`.\n\n## 2. `ValidatePostcode`\n- **[V]** If a postcode is present it must be 4 digits, and \u2014 for known city regions \u2014 within range: Sydney 2000\u20132099, Melbourne 3000\u20133099, Brisbane 4000\u20134099 (unknown city accepts any 4-digit). Otherwise \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException(\"postcode\")`. Absent postcode is left untouched.\n\n## 3. `AssignHouseholdId`\n- **[S]** If `sharesHousehold=true`, sets `householdId` = first 8 bytes of SHA-256 (hex) over `normalize(lastName)|normalize(address)`. No-op otherwise.\n\n## 4. `CheckUniqueIdentity`\n- **[V]** Builds `identityKey = telephone|email|householdId` and scans all owners; if another owner has the exact same key \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n\n## 5. `CheckCityCapacity`\n- **[V]** Counts existing owners in the same (normalized) city; if \u2265 50 \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n## 6. `AdjustRegistrationDate`\n- **[S]** If `registrationDate` lands on Saturday/Sunday, rolls it forward to the next Monday (mutates the owner). Runs before the daily-limit count and before the membership-number year is derived.\n\n## 7. `CheckDailyLimit`\n- **[V]** Counts owners already registered on that (possibly adjusted) `registrationDate`; if \u2265 100 \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429).\n\n## 8. `AssignCustomerCode`\n- **[S]** Sets `customerCode` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (upper-cased first 3 letters of city and last name; `NNNN` = count of owners already in that city + 1).\n\n## 9. `AssignNamesakeCount`\n- **[S]** Sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing the same first+last name (case-insensitive). Runs pre-save, so it counts only prior owners.\n\n## 10. `FlagBulkSignup`\n- **[S]** Sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if more than 80 owners were already registered today (by `registrationDate`).\n\n## 11. `SaveOwner`\n- **[S]** Persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns the `id`).\n\n## 12. `AuditOwnerCreated`\n- **[S]** Emits an `AUDIT` log line with `id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and derived `membershipLevel`.\n\n## 13. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n- **[S]** Maps to `OwnerDto` (deriving `displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey`) and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**A note on ordering:** validations are interleaved with side-effects rather than all up front. In particular, `BuildOwner` and `AssignHouseholdId` mutate/populate the entity *before* the uniqueness (`CheckUniqueIdentity`), capacity, and daily-limit checks \u2014 and because every step shares one transaction that commits at the end, a rejection at any check rolls the whole thing back, so no partial owner is persisted."
